33,2,1,talk,Shizue,,"It appears that while some ambitious projects have stalled, those focused on creating lasting catalogues have provided enduring value to the community.","{""words"":22,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
34,2,1,talk,Ryuji,,"My findings suggest a significant shortage of phenotyping technicians, though there is currently a healthy surplus of applicants for modelling and code-related positions.","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
35,2,1,talk,Victoria,,"I've discovered that while the animal facilities are well-supported, the spectroscopy suite suffered significant downtime recently, and the glasshouses are completely booked for the foreseeable future.","{""words"":26,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
36,2,1,talk,Benjamin,,"It seems the financial burden has shifted; while computing costs are centrally covered, animal-unit rates have risen sharply and shipping costs are climbing despite frozen per-diems.","{""words"":26,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
37,2,1,talk,Midori,,"I found that field sites have been quite vulnerable to environmental disasters lately, though the national repository has significantly improved its turnaround times for deposits.","{""words"":25,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
38,2,2,talk,Shizue,,"It is heartening to hear that the repository is efficient now, but I worry that our preference for ""mechanism"" research may be leading us toward those unresolved ends I saw in the files.","{""words"":33,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
39,2,2,talk,Ryuji,,"@Victoria, given the shortage of phenotyping technicians I found, does the booking status of the glasshouses suggest a bottleneck in personnel or simply a lack of physical space?","{""words"":28,""mentions"":[""Victoria""],""raw_differs"":false}"
40,2,2,talk,Victoria,,"@Ryuji, the records indicate the glasshouses are booked solid through two more growing cycles, which suggests a physical capacity limit regardless of the staffing levels.","{""words"":25,""mentions"":[""Ryuji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
41,2,2,talk,Benjamin,,"It is a curious intersection; we have a surplus of computational talent and covered costs, yet the physical infrastructure for botany is entirely saturated.","{""words"":24,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
42,2,2,talk,Midori,,"That is a very concerning point, Benjamin. If the glasshouses are full and field sites are unstable, any project relying on plant trials seems particularly risky right now.","{""words"":28,""mentions"":[""Benjamin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
43,2,3,talk,Shizue,,"I agree with Midori. If the physical space is unavailable and the environment is unpredictable, we must be very cautious about any proposal requiring extensive plant work.","{""words"":27,""mentions"":[""Midori""],""raw_differs"":false}"
44,2,3,talk,Ryuji,,"@Victoria, does the downtime in the spectroscopy suite seem like a recurring systemic failure, or was it a one-time lapse in the service contract?","{""words"":24,""mentions"":[""Victoria""],""raw_differs"":false}"
45,2,3,talk,Victoria,,"It was a lapse in the service contract, but the fact that one engineer now covers three institutes suggests a systemic fragility in maintenance that could easily recur.","{""words"":28,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
46,2,3,talk,Benjamin,,"So, we have a situation where the digital and computational paths are well-funded and staffed, while the physical, biological paths are fraught with logistical and maintenance risks.","{""words"":27,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
47,2,3,talk,Midori,,Exactly. It seems the safest and most productive path forward would be to favor projects that lean into those strengths rather than fighting the current infrastructure.,"{""words"":26,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
48,2,4,talk,Shizue,,I believe we are in agreement; we should prioritize stability and proven delivery over high-risk ambitions that the current infrastructure cannot support.,"{""words"":22,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
49,2,4,talk,Ryuji,,I concur. We should look for a proposal that aligns with the available technical staff and the current state of the facilities to ensure the grant is actually usable.,"{""words"":29,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
50,2,4,talk,Victoria,,I agree. We must avoid any project that would be crippled by the current spectroscopy maintenance issues or the lack of glasshouse availability.,"{""words"":23,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
51,2,4,talk,Benjamin,,"I suspect we shall find that the most ""elegant"" proposal on paper may be the most impractical in reality, given these constraints. I am ready to see the candidates.","{""words"":29,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
52,2,4,talk,Midori,,I am as well. Let us hope the candidates provide a path that balances scientific ambition with the practical realities we have uncovered.,"{""words"":23,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
